  data: {
    LLM: "Only buy cards when the improvement significantly helps your hand. Consider the cost vs potential return. With a weak hand showing, buying may be expensive as others may raise. In high-low, decide early which direction to pursue or whether to go for both.\n\nTrack visible cards to calculate odds of improving. Consider what opponents are buying - if they're buying high cards they likely want high; if buying low cards they want low. The 4-unit unknown card is risky but hides your intentions. Balance the cost of buying against the pot size.\n\nUse buying to mislead opponents - buying a face-up card reveals information. Sometimes buying a card you don't need can confuse opponents about your hand direction. Calculate expected value of each purchase based on pot odds and probability of winning. In declaration, read opponents' betting patterns to determine if they're going high, low, or both.",
    Player: "Only buy cards when the improvement significantly helps your hand. Consider the cost vs potential return. With a weak hand showing, buying may be expensive as others may raise. In high-low, decide early which direction to pursue or whether to go for both.\n\nTrack visible cards to calculate odds of improving. Consider what opponents are buying - if they're buying high cards they likely want high; if buying low cards they want low. The 4-unit unknown card is risky but hides your intentions. Balance the cost of buying against the pot size.\n\nUse buying to mislead opponents - buying a face-up card reveals information. Sometimes buying a card you don't need can confuse opponents about your hand direction. Calculate expected value of each purchase based on pot odds and probability of winning. In declaration, read opponents' betting patterns to determine if they're going high, low, or both.",
